      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c6bfb5fb_4537e210",
        "filename": "zephyr/drivers/usbc/pdc_rts54xx.c",
        "patchSetId": 35
      },
      "lineNbr": 2296,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-05-08T20:11:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m still concerned that the `rts54_post_command()` will call the `call_cci_event_cb()` when this synchronous command completes.  That can potentially corrupt state in the PDM.\n\nCan the PPM register a new callback using `pdc_set_handler_cb()` before starting the synchronous command?  You would need to trigger the PDM to re-register it\u0027s callback when done.\n\nThis would allow you to do the polling in the PPM layer instead of each driver.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2285,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 2296,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "bc0d78f542625dee7d29a3347cceae077671ca37",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a66f5283_5bfededf",
        "filename": "zephyr/drivers/usbc/pdc_rts54xx.c",
        "patchSetId": 35
      },
      "lineNbr": 2296,
      "author": {
        "id": 1365249
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-05-09T17:40:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I agree with your concern but disagree with the solution.\n\nThis driver overloads CCI_CB for two purposes -- one for the actual cmd response/result indication and another for the LPM alert. CCI is used for the OPM-PPM interface and doesn\u0027t quite fit into how things work with the Realtek board.\n\nThis driver needs to be refactored instead to separate command callbacks and alerts so that each API call must provide a callback for commands and each client must register a generic callback for connector change events.\n\n----\n\nWrt/ the race here:\n\n* pdc_power_mgmt only checks the CCI bits setting if sending a command (https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/zephyr/subsys/pd_controller/pdc_power_mgmt.c;l\u003d2013)\n* Calls in pdc_rts54xx are serialized such that you can only queue new commands after the previous one has gone fully idle (https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/zephyr/drivers/usbc/pdc_rts54xx.c;l\u003d871)\n\nExcept for the LPM alert (I.e. CCI_EVENT in pdc_power_mgmt), the other CCI indicators are no-ops in the power management code.\n\nWe can add the suggested refactor of callbacks to the top of the stack but that should not block this current `_sync` function from landing.",
      "parentUuid": "c6bfb5fb_4537e210",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2285,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 2296,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "bc0d78f542625dee7d29a3347cceae077671ca37",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b74fe065_b7921b50",
        "filename": "zephyr/drivers/usbc/pdc_rts54xx.c",
        "patchSetId": 35
      },
      "lineNbr": 2296,
      "author": {
        "id": 1106949
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-05-09T17:56:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Done.\n\n\u003e This would allow you to do the polling in the PPM layer instead of each driver.\n\nI\u0027m not sure whether this polling will be common or unique to RTS5453. We probably want to generalize the interface when we have more PDC drivers.",
      "parentUuid": "c6bfb5fb_4537e210",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2285,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 2296,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "bc0d78f542625dee7d29a3347cceae077671ca37",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
